AB  - Dam Safety Monitoring Systems (DSMSs) are crucial in evaluating the operational state of dams. However, heterogeneous monitoring data distributed from multiple sources during the dam operation lacks a unified data integration method and prohibits knowledge extraction and intelligent analysis, which currently poses a labor-intensive task. To address this issue, a solution relying on Building Information Modeling (BIM) and domain ontologies is proposed. Specifically, a DSMS domain ontology (OntoDSMS) is developed by comprehensively collecting domain knowledge and extracting context information from the dam information model. Furthermore, a rule-based reasoner and SPARQL queries are implemented. The proposed approach facilitates the effective integration of dam safety monitoring information while reducing retrieval time effectively compared with traditional databases. A case is illustrated to demonstrate the feasibility and practicality of the proposed approach. © 2022 Elsevier B.V.
